# Core Directives

On session start, read docs/START_HERE.md, pick Cursor mode via docs/CURSOR_MODES.md, then edit.

## Plan First, Code Second

- Cursor mode routing: see cursor-modes.mdc and docs/CURSOR_MODES.md
- Plan Mode for non-trivial tasks; Ask for read-only exploration
- Include mandatory `### Critique` in every plan as an **Issue → Resolution** table
- Every critique must have a concrete resolution (file, test, gate, BUILD_PLAN step, or `[HUMAN]` destructive-ops item) baked into the plan body — not open risks or “ask later”
- Pick a single best approach; do not dump unresolved alternatives on the human
- Bare “defer” / “monitor” / “optional later” is forbidden unless the resolution names a tracked follow-up and why shipping without it is safe now
- Ask the human only for `[HUMAN]` destructive-ops or facts undiscoverable from the codebase

## Read-Before-Write

- Inspect types/interfaces via @filename before altering code

## BUILD_PLAN Protocol

- Sequential lane before Parallel lane
- Respect AGENT, HUMAN, ADB, AUTO labels
- Status markers: 🔲 open · ✅ done · ❌ blocked (emoji, not `- [ ]` checkboxes — repo-wide; see `BUILD_PLAN.md` legend)

## 3-Strike Rule

Halt after 3 consecutive failed fix attempts; escalate to human.

## Memory Files

Update only at session start, milestone boundary, or architectural pivot.

## Token Economy

Max 300 lines static data (UI + i18n), 150 lines pure logic. Read active module/example only.

## Local Compute

On This Computer, prefer parallel Task/worktrees/`/best-of-n` and multi-core local gates over Cloud Agents — see `local-compute.mdc`.
